WEBVTT

1
00:00:41.611 --> 00:00:42.987
Time!

2
00:00:43.822 --> 00:00:44.823
Holy shit.

3
00:00:46.116 --> 00:00:47.325
- What is it?
- Guess.

4
00:00:49.285 --> 00:00:50.286
5:19?

5
00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:51.746
5:07.

6
00:00:53.456 --> 00:00:54.999
That's enough for Ridgewood?

7
00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:57.292
Yeah. That's almost enough
for the Olympics.

8
00:00:58.711 --> 00:01:00.087
Let's get you some dinner.

9
00:01:01.296 --> 00:01:02.881
- 5:07
- Yeah, man.

10
00:01:09.722 --> 00:01:10.556
Woo.

11
00:01:11.432 --> 00:01:12.850
Hey, how was it?

12
00:01:12.933 --> 00:01:15.561
We are in the presence
of a future Olympian.

13
00:01:17.062 --> 00:01:18.272
Just guess my time.

14
00:01:18.355 --> 00:01:20.065
Okay. Five...

15
00:01:20.149 --> 00:01:21.691
- 5:07.
- What?

16
00:01:21.774 --> 00:01:24.193
- 5:07.
- 5:07? That's incredible.

17
00:01:24.569 --> 00:01:26.195
- Right?
- That's my best.

18
00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.030
We made that.
Did you know we made you?

19
00:01:28.156 --> 00:01:29.782
- Okay.
- We made you with our bodies.

20
00:01:29.866 --> 00:01:31.284
- I know.
- Okay.

21
00:01:31.409 --> 00:01:34.078
Go take a shower.
I'm making breakfast for dinner.

22
00:02:07.486 --> 00:02:09.154
Oh, fuck.

23
00:02:11.198 --> 00:02:14.241
- It won't change until you talk to Jim.
- I gotta catch him on a good day.

24
00:02:14.325 --> 00:02:17.286
- He's in a bad mood.
- Yeah, he's always in a bad mood, Brian.

25
00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:20.372
- You just have to sit him down.
- Okay, I hear you, all right?

26
00:02:20.456 --> 00:02:22.416
Brian, I'm looking for work too, but...

27
00:02:23.417 --> 00:02:24.585
- There he is.
- Hey.

28
00:02:24.668 --> 00:02:27.630
- I'm gonna go get some eggs. Wanna come?
- Sure.

29
00:02:27.755 --> 00:02:29.924
Hey, get milk, too, okay?

30
00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.311
- God.
- Right?

31
00:02:43.394 --> 00:02:45.271
- Yeah. It's fucking great.
- Yeah, I'm obsessed.

32
00:02:46.731 --> 00:02:47.941
All right. I'm going in.

33
00:02:48.441 --> 00:02:50.068
You staying? Or are you going?

34
00:02:50.151 --> 00:02:51.444
- I'm staying.
- Okay.

35
00:02:56.866 --> 00:02:58.785
Hey. Can you bring me something?

36
00:02:59.244 --> 00:03:00.537
I'll think about it.

37
00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.798
- Hey, Tommy.
- Hey, man.

38
00:03:35.194 --> 00:03:36.028
No!

39
00:03:59.593 --> 00:04:01.928
I guess the driver had a heart attack.

40
00:04:02.262 --> 00:04:03.638
- It's awful.
- Yes.

41
00:04:09.644 --> 00:04:10.520
Logan?

42
00:04:14.274 --> 00:04:15.108
Yeah?

43
00:04:19.945 --> 00:04:21.196
The Kellmans are leaving.

44
00:04:25.409 --> 00:04:26.243
Okay.

45
00:04:40.507 --> 00:04:41.967
Are you guys gonna stay here?

46
00:04:45.887 --> 00:04:47.180
I can't afford the rent.

47
00:04:48.056 --> 00:04:49.474
With me being out of work and now...

48
00:04:51.142 --> 00:04:53.519
You should stay at our mountain house.

49
00:04:55.021 --> 00:04:57.690
- No.
- No, I'm serious, Naomi.

50
00:04:57.815 --> 00:04:59.776
I mean, it's just sitting there, and...

51
00:05:00.193 --> 00:05:02.320
You know that Bruce won't have
a problem with it.

52
00:05:03.363 --> 00:05:04.405
I want to help.

53
00:05:07.241 --> 00:05:08.701
I thought you guys were selling...

54
00:05:09.369 --> 00:05:10.953
We are, but...

55
00:05:11.703 --> 00:05:14.915
You just have to leave for a bit
on Sundays during open houses.

56
00:05:18.377 --> 00:05:20.337
- It's nothing.
- I don't know, Ally.

57
00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:23.048
- Having people living there is not...
- It'll be fine.

58
00:05:24.091 --> 00:05:26.885
Okay? You can look after the place.

59
00:05:28.387 --> 00:05:31.598
Logan would kill me if I pulled him
out of school right now.

60
00:05:32.182 --> 00:05:35.060
Okay, look, it's just until
you get back on your feet.

61
00:05:35.143 --> 00:05:36.686
And you'll come back.

62
00:05:39.563 --> 00:05:40.690
I just can't believe it.

63
00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:42.483
He's dead.

64
00:05:59.083 --> 00:06:00.334
Okay.

65
00:06:03.962 --> 00:06:04.796
Ready?

66
00:06:07.007 --> 00:06:07.841
Yep.

67
00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:52.382
No, you're not listening
to what I'm saying.

68
00:06:53.341 --> 00:06:54.968
I am the executor.

69
00:06:57.721 --> 00:07:00.515
Well, yes. He was my husband.

70
00:07:02.934 --> 00:07:03.769
What?

71
00:07:06.146 --> 00:07:07.022
Hello?

72
00:07:07.355 --> 00:07:08.231
Hello?

73
00:07:08.523 --> 00:07:09.816
Can you hear me?

74
00:07:10.984 --> 00:07:11.860
Hello?

75
00:07:14.196 --> 00:07:15.113
Damn it.

76
00:07:32.129 --> 00:07:34.006
How long did you say
we were gonna be here for?

77
00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:36.967
- I don't know, Logan.
- You said I'd be back before graduation.

78
00:07:37.051 --> 00:07:40.346
I said I don't know,
and I'm gonna do my best, okay?

79
00:07:48.645 --> 00:07:51.481
Can you pass me my phone?
It's at your feet.

80
00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:02.200
Hey, Mom! Shit!

81
00:08:04.035 --> 00:08:06.538
Oh, sh...! Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

82
00:08:06.621 --> 00:08:08.414
Please tell me he's okay.

83
00:08:11.333 --> 00:08:12.751
He's... he's not there.

84
00:08:14.086 --> 00:08:14.920
What?

85
00:08:27.099 --> 00:08:28.725
Hey, let's just... let's just go.

86
00:08:29.601 --> 00:08:30.477
What?

87
00:08:31.603 --> 00:08:32.855
I could have killed him.

88
00:08:35.857 --> 00:08:37.066
Mom, your nose.

89
00:08:38.651 --> 00:08:39.527
Oh, shit.

90
00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:40.528
Hey, uh...

91
00:08:41.571 --> 00:08:42.530
Here.

92
00:08:43.739 --> 00:08:44.615
Here.

93
00:08:45.074 --> 00:08:46.534
It's just the altitude.

94
00:09:40.127 --> 00:09:41.295
Oh, shit.

95
00:09:41.754 --> 00:09:44.131
- Sorry.
- Oh, no worry at all, honey.

96
00:09:44.215 --> 00:09:45.216
Wait a minute.

97
00:09:45.799 --> 00:09:48.052
You must be Logan.

98
00:09:48.636 --> 00:09:49.595
Hi?

99
00:09:49.887 --> 00:09:52.055
Oh, and hold on...

100
00:09:52.138 --> 00:09:53.014
Naomi.

101
00:09:53.514 --> 00:09:57.227
- I'm sorry?
- Oh, forgive me. I'm Martha.

102
00:09:57.977 --> 00:09:59.437
Bruce and Allison's neighbor.

103
00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.148
She told me her sister and nephew
were coming in.

104
00:10:02.232 --> 00:10:06.110
She emailed me a picture,
so I knew exactly who you two were.

105
00:10:06.194 --> 00:10:07.487
Oh, okay.

106
00:10:09.239 --> 00:10:11.699
So sorry for what happened
to your husband.

107
00:10:12.408 --> 00:10:14.410
Allison told me all about it.

108
00:10:14.827 --> 00:10:16.370
So gruesome.

109
00:10:17.079 --> 00:10:18.664
You must miss him dearly.

110
00:10:19.206 --> 00:10:20.707
Yeah, we... we do.

111
00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:23.919
I lost my husband a few years back.

112
00:10:24.336 --> 00:10:27.547
Not a day goes by
that I don't feel the void.

113
00:10:28.632 --> 00:10:31.093
- Mom, should we...
- Oh. Oh, yes.

114
00:10:31.301 --> 00:10:33.470
I won't keep you any longer.
If you need anything,

115
00:10:33.553 --> 00:10:35.973
my house is just west through
the woods. You can't miss it.

116
00:10:36.056 --> 00:10:37.975
Thank you.
It's very kind of you.

117
00:10:38.058 --> 00:10:40.519
It's always nice to know
you have someone nearby.

118
00:10:41.228 --> 00:10:43.646
The quiet out here can get real loud.

119
00:10:45.064 --> 00:10:46.065
Buh-bye now.

120
00:10:58.536 --> 00:10:59.537
You okay?

121
00:11:01.038 --> 00:11:01.914
Yeah.

122
00:11:33.819 --> 00:11:35.404
Oh. Whoa.

123
00:11:35.487 --> 00:11:36.322
Yeah.

124
00:11:37.781 --> 00:11:41.577
Leave it to Ally to have
the biggest house on the mountain.

125
00:11:45.497 --> 00:11:47.916
How have we never been here before?
It's fucking huge.

126
00:11:48.042 --> 00:11:49.043
Language.

127
00:11:52.171 --> 00:11:53.047
But yeah.

128
00:11:54.214 --> 00:11:55.674
It is huge.

129
00:11:56.467 --> 00:11:57.968
Okay. Let's go.

130
00:12:26.703 --> 00:12:27.579
Well...

131
00:12:30.665 --> 00:12:32.084
Home sweet home.

132
00:12:56.315 --> 00:12:57.149
Hello?

133
00:12:59.151 --> 00:13:00.569
Uh, yes.

134
00:13:01.529 --> 00:13:02.696
Just got in.

135
00:13:05.074 --> 00:13:06.283
Oh, okay.

136
00:13:07.827 --> 00:13:08.744
Thanks.

137
00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:12.998
Who was that?

138
00:13:13.082 --> 00:13:14.083
Martha...

139
00:13:14.542 --> 00:13:15.583
the neighbor.

140
00:13:15.834 --> 00:13:16.668
Just...

141
00:13:17.043 --> 00:13:19.045
calling to see if we got in okay.

142
00:13:20.922 --> 00:13:23.425
I was kind of hoping
I wouldn't have reception up here.

143
00:13:25.051 --> 00:13:25.885
Hello?

144
00:13:27.011 --> 00:13:27.846
Oh.

145
00:13:28.638 --> 00:13:29.472
Hi.

146
00:13:30.473 --> 00:13:31.474
Oh, no, no.

147
00:13:32.559 --> 00:13:33.560
Well, you know...

148
00:13:34.185 --> 00:13:36.354
we've been driving all night, so...

149
00:13:41.817 --> 00:13:43.318
But, yeah...

150
00:13:43.402 --> 00:13:44.570
Yeah, I know.

151
00:13:45.654 --> 00:13:46.613
He's okay.

152
00:13:47.406 --> 00:13:48.282
I know.

153
00:13:49.533 --> 00:13:51.368
We're at my sister's house.

154
00:13:52.619 --> 00:13:55.289
It's a big, nice house.

155
00:13:55.789 --> 00:13:57.040
I think he likes it.

156
00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:10.225
Jesus.

157
00:17:34.207 --> 00:17:35.083
Logan?

158
00:17:36.417 --> 00:17:37.251
Yeah?

159
00:17:37.794 --> 00:17:39.295
Did you get a chance to sleep today?

160
00:17:40.672 --> 00:17:42.048
Not... not really.

161
00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:44.676
Well, you'll sleep like a rock tonight.

162
00:17:46.761 --> 00:17:48.554
First open house is tomorrow,

163
00:17:48.638 --> 00:17:50.932
so we gotta be out of here by 11:00, okay?

164
00:17:52.684 --> 00:17:53.517
Okay.

165
00:17:54.267 --> 00:17:57.186
Honey, are you sure you don't want to keep
that stuff in my room?

166
00:17:57.269 --> 00:17:58.270
No, no, it's okay.

167
00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:00.815
Okay.

168
00:18:01.982 --> 00:18:03.317
Well, I'm gonna head to bed.

169
00:18:05.277 --> 00:18:06.112
Love you.

170
00:20:32.752 --> 00:20:33.837
Who are you?

171
00:20:34.879 --> 00:20:36.840
What are you doing on our property?

172
00:20:37.423 --> 00:20:38.258
Ma'am?

173
00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:40.635
What do you want?

174
00:20:42.178 --> 00:20:43.972
Ma'am, this is our house.

175
00:20:44.848 --> 00:20:46.474
- Do you need help?
- No!

176
00:20:46.558 --> 00:20:47.600
Oh, God!

177
00:22:14.099 --> 00:22:17.561
You need to get up right now.
The open house is starting in 15 minutes.

178
00:22:17.645 --> 00:22:20.522
Ed, come on. You gotta get
the sign-in sheet out of the car.

179
00:22:20.606 --> 00:22:23.275
- You kidding me?
- The open house ends at five.

180
00:22:23.359 --> 00:22:25.110
Ed is gonna be running the show today,

181
00:22:25.194 --> 00:22:28.322
which means he will turn off
all the lights, he'll lock up.

182
00:22:28.405 --> 00:22:31.283
And Ed, don't forget
to leave the key under the mat.

183
00:22:31.367 --> 00:22:32.242
Got it.

184
00:22:32.534 --> 00:22:34.203
Oh, okay.

185
00:22:34.286 --> 00:22:36.204
- And do I need to do...
- Oh, God, no, no.

186
00:22:36.287 --> 00:22:38.706
You don't have to do a thing,
except one:

187
00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:41.876
Do not come back here until after five,

188
00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:46.130
because we do not want to upset
any potential buyers.

189
00:22:46.214 --> 00:22:48.508
- Mom, why didn't you wake me up?
- Oh, sorry.

190
00:22:48.591 --> 00:22:51.219
- I got a call and then I didn't...
- They scared the hell out of me.

191
00:22:51.302 --> 00:22:52.679
Ed, make his bed.

192
00:22:55.598 --> 00:22:59.018
You two really have to get going.
Really. Now.

193
00:23:19.871 --> 00:23:21.248
Hey, hey. No, hey.

194
00:23:26.294 --> 00:23:27.336
Welcome.

195
00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:30.548
And if you have any further questions
today, just sign in right there,

196
00:23:30.631 --> 00:23:33.259
and otherwise,
take a cookie, look around,

197
00:23:33.342 --> 00:23:34.885
and, uh, I'm here to help.

198
00:23:50.401 --> 00:23:52.652
So, why would she knock?

199
00:23:53.403 --> 00:23:54.487
She's nuts.

200
00:23:55.238 --> 00:23:56.698
Maybe she was lost.

201
00:23:58.867 --> 00:24:01.453
I just don't think the people up here
know what privacy is.

202
00:24:01.995 --> 00:24:05.373
Excuse me? Your card was declined.
Do you have another one we could use?

203
00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:07.625
Oh.

204
00:24:09.085 --> 00:24:10.253
Uh, you know what?

205
00:24:10.795 --> 00:24:11.963
I'll just use cash.

206
00:24:12.338 --> 00:24:13.214
Okay.

207
00:24:19.303 --> 00:24:20.220
Here. I-I got it.

208
00:24:20.304 --> 00:24:21.847
No. Honey, you don't even...

209
00:24:26.685 --> 00:24:27.895
It's birthday money.

210
00:24:29.313 --> 00:24:31.774
- Uh, here you go. No change.
- Thanks.

211
00:24:36.445 --> 00:24:37.988
Where'd you get birthday money?

212
00:24:38.822 --> 00:24:39.907
Aunt Allison.

213
00:24:42.493 --> 00:24:43.493
It's okay.

214
00:24:48.122 --> 00:24:49.040
Thank you.

215
00:24:58.424 --> 00:25:00.885
You know what?
Let's play a game.

216
00:25:01.511 --> 00:25:03.554
- What?
- Yeah. Come on, it'll be fun.

217
00:25:03.638 --> 00:25:05.556
Uh, if you won the lottery...

218
00:25:07.058 --> 00:25:08.892
what would you do with the winnings?

219
00:25:10.018 --> 00:25:11.186
I don't wanna play.

220
00:25:12.604 --> 00:25:13.688
Come on.

221
00:25:14.731 --> 00:25:15.732
Amuse me.

222
00:25:16.608 --> 00:25:17.651
Fine. Uh...

223
00:25:18.443 --> 00:25:19.319
I'd...

224
00:25:20.445 --> 00:25:21.905
I'd pay off our debt.

225
00:25:23.782 --> 00:25:24.616
Okay.

226
00:25:24.699 --> 00:25:26.076
We're not that bad off.

227
00:25:27.077 --> 00:25:28.286
But I would let you.

228
00:25:31.081 --> 00:25:32.916
I'd buy us a new house back home.

229
00:25:34.583 --> 00:25:36.293
- Can we have a pool?
- And a track.

230
00:25:37.837 --> 00:25:40.089
I'd go to the Olympics in Japan.

231
00:25:40.756 --> 00:25:42.883
- Can I come with you?
- Yeah. First class.

232
00:25:43.300 --> 00:25:45.845
Other than that, I'd probably
just give the rest to you.

233
00:25:47.555 --> 00:25:48.389
No.

234
00:25:49.265 --> 00:25:50.474
I don't need it. You...

235
00:25:52.476 --> 00:25:54.854
You'd probably spend it
on things that matter.

236
00:25:56.981 --> 00:25:58.691
Well, I personally think that...

237
00:26:01.151 --> 00:26:03.111
your dream of going to the Olympics

238
00:26:03.194 --> 00:26:06.030
and owning a home
with the biggest backyard ever

239
00:26:07.115 --> 00:26:08.741
are things that matter.

240
00:26:10.118 --> 00:26:11.035
Thanks.

241
00:26:12.328 --> 00:26:13.746
Okay. My turn.

242
00:26:14.789 --> 00:26:15.874
Debt.

243
00:26:18.459 --> 00:26:19.961
And then I think I would...

244
00:26:20.795 --> 00:26:22.422
start doing photography again.

245
00:26:22.797 --> 00:26:25.716
- Really?
- Yeah. I think so. I used to love it.

246
00:26:28.385 --> 00:26:29.761
You should...

247
00:26:30.637 --> 00:26:32.097
You should start again now.

248
00:26:33.098 --> 00:26:34.349
- Please.
- You should.

249
00:26:34.433 --> 00:26:36.727
You don't have to win the lottery
to do that.

250
00:26:37.603 --> 00:26:39.021
Now you sound like your dad.

251
00:26:55.745 --> 00:26:57.580
I don't think I've seen you before.

252
00:26:57.663 --> 00:27:00.541
Oh. Oh, yeah.
We've been getting a lot of that.

253
00:27:00.625 --> 00:27:01.667
Oh, yeah.

254
00:27:01.751 --> 00:27:04.086
Everybody knows everybody
in these small towns, huh?

255
00:27:04.587 --> 00:27:06.881
Mm-hmm. I have noticed.

256
00:27:07.798 --> 00:27:09.467
It's good to see some new faces.

257
00:27:10.134 --> 00:27:11.928
Especially pretty ones.

258
00:27:12.011 --> 00:27:14.472
I just mean the mountain folk
can get a little, uh...

259
00:27:14.555 --> 00:27:17.515
scruffy at times,
and I am not talking about the men.

260
00:27:20.060 --> 00:27:21.144
Whereabouts are you from?

261
00:27:21.853 --> 00:27:24.689
- Uh, well, we're from California.
- Mom, can we go?

262
00:27:24.773 --> 00:27:26.524
Hey, buddy. How you doing?

263
00:27:29.319 --> 00:27:30.403
Mom?

264
00:27:32.280 --> 00:27:34.783
- Uh, I'm so sorry.
- No.

265
00:27:55.427 --> 00:27:56.845
You didn't have to be rude.

266
00:28:00.891 --> 00:28:02.226
You were flirting.

267
00:28:03.310 --> 00:28:04.228
Logan...

268
00:28:05.562 --> 00:28:08.147
He was just talking to me.
I was being friendly.

269
00:28:12.610 --> 00:28:13.903
Are we allowed to go in yet?

270
00:28:15.571 --> 00:28:16.447
Yeah.

271
00:28:17.031 --> 00:28:18.533
Said it was over at five.

272
00:28:33.505 --> 00:28:36.258
- There's no key.
- What? Is it unlocked?

273
00:28:41.888 --> 00:28:42.764
Hello?

274
00:29:06.203 --> 00:29:07.288
Oh, Jesus!

275
00:29:07.747 --> 00:29:09.290
- Oh!
- Did you not... did you not hear us?

276
00:29:09.373 --> 00:29:11.500
Sorry. I was just locking everything up.

277
00:29:11.584 --> 00:29:12.710
We ran long.

278
00:29:12.793 --> 00:29:15.379
Uh, Jonie's picking me up right now,
so I, uh...

279
00:29:15.463 --> 00:29:18.424
I'm rushing, but your keys...
I left them right there,

280
00:29:18.507 --> 00:29:20.843
and, um, that should be everything.

281
00:29:21.385 --> 00:29:24.512
Okay? So, um... have... have a great night.

282
00:29:25.805 --> 00:29:26.681
Thank you.

283
00:29:33.396 --> 00:29:34.564
Turn on the light.

284
00:29:40.486 --> 00:29:41.403
Mom.

285
00:29:42.363 --> 00:29:45.574
Have you ever thought about
how, like, weird open houses are?

286
00:29:45.908 --> 00:29:46.742
What?

287
00:29:48.118 --> 00:29:50.828
I mean, you give your keys
to someone you hardly know,

288
00:29:51.329 --> 00:29:54.624
they stand in one room and welcome in
a bunch of complete strangers,

289
00:29:54.707 --> 00:29:57.585
and those people
just roam around the house.

290
00:29:58.086 --> 00:30:00.505
And the realtor doesn't check the house
when it's done, right?

291
00:30:00.588 --> 00:30:03.091
They just... turn the lights off and go?

292
00:30:03.925 --> 00:30:06.844
Okay, well, now I'm not
gonna sleep tonight.

293
00:30:10.431 --> 00:30:12.141
Maybe you shouldn't sleep tonight.

294
00:30:13.309 --> 00:30:14.268
Stop.

295
00:30:45.923 --> 00:30:48.426
But a suicide generally leaves a note.

296
00:30:48.509 --> 00:30:51.429
Well, this one didn't.
Probably didn't have time.

297
00:30:53.305 --> 00:30:54.223
I have to pee.

298
00:30:55.307 --> 00:30:56.142
Okay.

299
00:31:42.436 --> 00:31:43.687
Just gonna watch it ring?

300
00:31:46.231 --> 00:31:47.065
Hello?

301
00:31:49.193 --> 00:31:50.027
Hello?

302
00:31:51.778 --> 00:31:52.779
Who is it?

303
00:31:53.906 --> 00:31:54.740
It...

304
00:31:55.157 --> 00:31:56.200
Can you hear me?

305
00:31:56.283 --> 00:31:57.492
Is anyone there?

306
00:32:01.996 --> 00:32:03.623
- What?
- It's just us.

307
00:32:03.706 --> 00:32:05.374
Like, I could just hear echoing.

308
00:32:14.592 --> 00:32:16.969
Or they might have been
in South America...

309
00:33:27.954 --> 00:33:29.622
Hey, Mom, have you seen my phone?

310
00:33:30.081 --> 00:33:32.834
Uh... no. Sorry, babe.

311
00:33:33.167 --> 00:33:34.002
I haven't.

312
00:33:35.461 --> 00:33:37.046
I'm gonna use yours real quick.

313
00:33:37.380 --> 00:33:38.214
Okay.

314
00:35:03.045 --> 00:35:05.130
- Logan!
- Oh, shoot! Sorry, Mom. God.

315
00:35:06.799 --> 00:35:08.008
You scared me.

316
00:35:08.092 --> 00:35:10.803
The water is ice cold.
I have to go check the tank.

317
00:35:10.886 --> 00:35:13.055
- Wait, that's in the basement.
- I know.

318
00:35:13.847 --> 00:35:17.559
- I heard something banging down there.
- Yeah, it's probably the old pipes.

319
00:36:21.537 --> 00:36:22.747
Oh, come on.

320
00:36:33.716 --> 00:36:34.800
Ugh.

321
00:36:34.884 --> 00:36:35.926
Jesus.

322
00:36:36.010 --> 00:36:36.885
Okay.

323
00:36:54.319 --> 00:36:55.195
Logan?

324
00:37:03.327 --> 00:37:04.411
Logan?

325
00:37:08.791 --> 00:37:10.250
That's not funny, Logan.

326
00:37:10.334 --> 00:37:12.753
- What?
- You slammed the basement door on me.

327
00:37:13.629 --> 00:37:15.506
I have no idea what you're talking about.

328
00:37:25.140 --> 00:37:26.391
Maybe the door is broken.

329
00:37:57.295 --> 00:37:58.797
Time!

330
00:37:58.880 --> 00:38:00.382
5:34.

331
00:38:01.258 --> 00:38:03.260
- Nice.
- It needs to be faster.

332
00:38:03.343 --> 00:38:05.095
What? That's great.

333
00:38:05.178 --> 00:38:08.265
No. Come on, you don't get it.
It needs to be faster.

334
00:38:08.348 --> 00:38:12.310
Honey, you're on a mountain.
Maybe you ran more than a mile.

335
00:38:12.394 --> 00:38:14.479
No, I mapped it out.

336
00:38:15.480 --> 00:38:17.524
Are you sure you started
the second I left?

337
00:38:18.816 --> 00:38:20.568
You can do it yourself if you want.

338
00:38:30.870 --> 00:38:32.288
Did you find your phone yet?

339
00:38:33.330 --> 00:38:35.583
No, it's gone.

340
00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:38.544
Well, it's not gone.
It has to be somewhere.

341
00:38:39.920 --> 00:38:41.589
- I don't know.
- Who's that?

342
00:38:52.140 --> 00:38:52.974
Hey.

343
00:38:54.017 --> 00:38:54.851
Hey.

344
00:38:55.977 --> 00:38:56.811
Oh...

345
00:38:57.520 --> 00:38:58.521
It's you guys.

346
00:38:59.397 --> 00:39:01.399
- What are you doing here?
- Right.

347
00:39:01.900 --> 00:39:02.942
This looks bad.

348
00:39:03.234 --> 00:39:05.945
I was just on the back roads,
saw the "For Sale" sign.

349
00:39:07.113 --> 00:39:08.489
Honey.

350
00:39:09.157 --> 00:39:10.032
Logan.

351
00:39:13.994 --> 00:39:15.954
I'm sorry. He's, uh...

352
00:39:16.038 --> 00:39:18.332
No, no need to apologize. I can relate.

353
00:39:18.957 --> 00:39:22.461
- You have teenagers?
- No, but I was one once.

354
00:39:23.795 --> 00:39:27.132
Well, this is my sister's house.
We're just staying here for a bit.

355
00:39:27.215 --> 00:39:28.091
Lucky us.

356
00:39:28.675 --> 00:39:31.136
Yeah. Um, you could call the realtors.

357
00:39:31.720 --> 00:39:33.639
They're the ones that set up the showings.

358
00:39:33.722 --> 00:39:35.473
Got it. Thank you.

359
00:39:36.057 --> 00:39:36.933
I'll do that.

360
00:39:39.936 --> 00:39:40.895
You know what?

361
00:39:42.104 --> 00:39:43.314
While we're here...

362
00:39:43.814 --> 00:39:46.192
would there be any way at all
I can just peek inside?

363
00:39:54.492 --> 00:39:56.619
- So you looking to move?
- Thinking about it.

364
00:39:57.954 --> 00:39:59.830
I'd kill for this kind of privacy.

365
00:40:02.457 --> 00:40:03.959
I don't think I caught your name.

366
00:40:04.042 --> 00:40:05.085
Uh, Naomi.

367
00:40:05.168 --> 00:40:07.629
Naomi. It's nice to meet you. I'm Chris.

368
00:40:08.088 --> 00:40:11.633
Well, I'll let you do your thing.
Don't mind me.

369
00:40:12.092 --> 00:40:12.968
Great.

370
00:41:16.612 --> 00:41:17.571
No!

371
00:41:22.283 --> 00:41:23.117
Chris?

372
00:41:24.994 --> 00:41:25.828
Hello?

373
00:41:30.916 --> 00:41:32.168
Who are you talking to?

374
00:41:32.251 --> 00:41:33.919
Um, that guy...

375
00:41:34.003 --> 00:41:36.589
wanted to see the house
since he missed yesterday.

376
00:41:37.590 --> 00:41:38.883
He's still here?

377
00:41:38.966 --> 00:41:42.011
He's probably left.
He was just looking around.

378
00:41:42.595 --> 00:41:44.137
I was in my room.

379
00:41:48.183 --> 00:41:49.059
Logan?

380
00:43:23.859 --> 00:43:25.317
Okay.

381
00:43:26.485 --> 00:43:29.530
What do you want to have
with your mac and cheese?

382
00:43:30.281 --> 00:43:31.740
Hot dogs?

383
00:43:31.824 --> 00:43:33.409
Or...

384
00:43:37.621 --> 00:43:38.581
hot dogs?

385
00:43:40.583 --> 00:43:42.168
I'd have to say hot dogs.

386
00:43:42.585 --> 00:43:43.419
Great.

387
00:43:50.217 --> 00:43:51.092
I'll get it.

388
00:44:01.227 --> 00:44:02.812
Hello there, neighbor.

389
00:44:02.896 --> 00:44:04.397
Uh, hi, um...

390
00:44:04.480 --> 00:44:05.398
- Martha.
- Martha.

391
00:44:05.481 --> 00:44:08.484
That's okay, Naomi.
I won't hold it against you.

392
00:44:08.568 --> 00:44:12.488
Oh, my goodness. I love this little house.

393
00:44:12.572 --> 00:44:14.699
So nice to see it lived in again.

394
00:44:15.200 --> 00:44:18.911
I can't tell you how sad I was
when I saw that "For Sale" sign go up.

395
00:44:19.453 --> 00:44:22.414
It's definitely a beautiful home.

396
00:44:23.290 --> 00:44:25.626
I'd feel awkward if I didn't tell you...

397
00:44:27.794 --> 00:44:29.755
We came to the open house yesterday.

398
00:44:30.589 --> 00:44:34.009
We just wanted to see the place
one last time

399
00:44:34.092 --> 00:44:36.720
before some stranger snatches it up.

400
00:44:37.221 --> 00:44:38.805
Oh, okay. Yeah...

401
00:44:38.889 --> 00:44:42.642
Oh, I almost forgot.
I do that a lot these days.

402
00:44:42.725 --> 00:44:45.019
Uh... I brought you banana bread.

403
00:44:45.102 --> 00:44:47.730
You and Logan are gonna love it.
Everybody does.

404
00:44:47.813 --> 00:44:48.773
Thank you.

405
00:44:48.856 --> 00:44:51.067
Where is that handsome young boy?

406
00:44:51.150 --> 00:44:53.861
- Oh, he's in the kitchen.
- Oh.

407
00:44:53.945 --> 00:44:56.072
We're making dinner, so...

408
00:44:57.990 --> 00:44:58.866
Well...

409
00:44:59.367 --> 00:45:02.161
I just was gonna swing by
and check in on you.

410
00:45:02.995 --> 00:45:05.623
If you need anything,
don't hesitate to come by.

411
00:45:05.706 --> 00:45:07.791
My husband can't wait
to meet the two of you.

412
00:45:10.502 --> 00:45:12.087
I'm sorry, um...

413
00:45:12.170 --> 00:45:13.338
but I thought...

414
00:45:14.005 --> 00:45:17.133
I thought you had said
your husband passed away.

415
00:45:17.217 --> 00:45:18.510
Passed away?

416
00:45:20.053 --> 00:45:21.221
Oh.

417
00:45:21.304 --> 00:45:24.015
Why would I say something silly like that?

418
00:45:25.141 --> 00:45:28.019
No, no. The Devil himself
couldn't slow him down.

419
00:45:28.645 --> 00:45:29.938
You have yourself a good one.

420
00:45:31.773 --> 00:45:32.731
Buh-bye.

421
00:45:33.941 --> 00:45:34.984
Bye, Martha.

422
00:45:50.958 --> 00:45:52.042
Shit.

423
00:45:54.962 --> 00:45:56.046
Ugh.

424
00:47:09.575 --> 00:47:10.618
Logan!

425
00:48:01.083 --> 00:48:02.000
Oh, fuck.

426
00:50:53.373 --> 00:50:55.208
Ally, I was married to a plumber
for 16 years.

427
00:50:55.292 --> 00:50:57.085
I think I know
when a water heater is broken.

428
00:51:01.047 --> 00:51:02.007
Thank you.

429
00:51:24.153 --> 00:51:25.029
Logan?

430
00:51:26.113 --> 00:51:28.490
Logan, sweetheart. Are you okay?

431
00:51:30.450 --> 00:51:31.326
I'm fine.

432
00:51:31.409 --> 00:51:33.536
Oh, honey. Let me walk you home.

433
00:51:34.454 --> 00:51:35.913
No, no, that's all right.

434
00:51:35.997 --> 00:51:37.373
Nonsense. Come on.

435
00:51:38.499 --> 00:51:39.459
Come on.

436
00:51:48.176 --> 00:51:49.594
Where did you come from?

437
00:51:49.677 --> 00:51:53.431
Oh, I always like to start my day
with a nice stroll through the forest.

438
00:51:54.307 --> 00:51:56.350
The nature... the air...

439
00:51:57.476 --> 00:51:59.102
How you liking the neighborhood?

440
00:52:01.813 --> 00:52:02.856
It's fine.

441
00:52:03.523 --> 00:52:06.234
Just hoping that the house sells soon
so that we can go home.

442
00:52:06.318 --> 00:52:08.737
You're not going anywhere
anytime soon.

443
00:52:10.280 --> 00:52:13.200
I'm sure of it.
Houses up here take some time to sell.

444
00:52:21.666 --> 00:52:22.792
What happened?

445
00:52:23.459 --> 00:52:24.710
I'm... I'm fine.

446
00:52:24.794 --> 00:52:27.088
Poor boy got sick on his run.

447
00:52:27.672 --> 00:52:29.882
But not to worry. I was watching on.

448
00:52:30.299 --> 00:52:32.593
- Are you okay, honey?
- It was just a cramp.

449
00:52:32.677 --> 00:52:35.596
Nothing that a hot shower
and a good breakfast can't fix.

450
00:52:36.013 --> 00:52:37.348
Well, thank you, Martha.

451
00:52:37.431 --> 00:52:38.683
I appreciate it.

452
00:52:38.766 --> 00:52:39.809
Hey, um...

453
00:52:40.601 --> 00:52:43.020
I hope you're both doing all right.

454
00:52:44.397 --> 00:52:45.272
Death...

455
00:52:46.815 --> 00:52:49.150
It's like it moves in and...

456
00:52:49.818 --> 00:52:51.069
never leaves.

457
00:52:55.073 --> 00:52:55.949
Buh-bye now.

458
00:53:03.915 --> 00:53:05.125
She's so weird.

459
00:53:18.136 --> 00:53:19.512
I'm here for the water heater.

460
00:53:19.595 --> 00:53:22.348
- Great. Uh, it's just in the...
- In the basement, right?

461
00:53:22.849 --> 00:53:24.600
- Yeah.
- I've been here before.

462
00:54:14.106 --> 00:54:14.940
Ma'am?

463
00:54:15.024 --> 00:54:16.066
- Oh! Oh, my God!
- Sorry.

464
00:54:16.150 --> 00:54:18.527
Oh, shit. Sorry. Um...

465
00:54:18.611 --> 00:54:19.570
I didn't hear you.

466
00:54:20.905 --> 00:54:23.157
- How did it look down there?
- Normal.

467
00:54:23.240 --> 00:54:25.326
Relit the pilot. It's burning.

468
00:54:25.785 --> 00:54:28.912
Then I changed the thermal coupler.
You should be good to go.

469
00:54:28.995 --> 00:54:29.829
Okay.

470
00:54:31.080 --> 00:54:33.333
- Wll, sorry for the inconvenience.
- No, not at all.

471
00:54:33.416 --> 00:54:34.834
I'm out here almost daily.

472
00:54:34.918 --> 00:54:37.879
This Martha down the road,
she lost her husband a few months back.

473
00:54:37.962 --> 00:54:40.006
She gets kind of sad.
I think she'd flood her house

474
00:54:40.089 --> 00:54:42.133
if it meant me stopping by
for a few hours.

475
00:54:43.343 --> 00:54:45.428
So, her husband did die.

476
00:54:45.512 --> 00:54:47.180
What, she told you something different?

477
00:54:47.764 --> 00:54:48.598
Yeah.

478
00:54:48.973 --> 00:54:49.891
Yeah.

479
00:54:50.517 --> 00:54:53.519
She got Alzheimer's a few months back,
so she gets things

480
00:54:53.602 --> 00:54:55.646
a little confused from time to time.

481
00:54:57.189 --> 00:54:58.398
- That's terrible.
- Yeah.

482
00:54:58.482 --> 00:55:00.526
Oh. And hey, I, uh...

483
00:55:00.609 --> 00:55:03.862
I found this by the water heater.

484
00:55:05.072 --> 00:55:06.740
Thought you might be looking for it.

485
00:55:15.666 --> 00:55:16.500
Found your phone.

486
00:55:18.918 --> 00:55:20.169
Okay. Well, where was it?

487
00:55:20.253 --> 00:55:22.672
In the basement next to the water heater.

488
00:55:25.216 --> 00:55:26.092
Oh.

489
00:55:26.676 --> 00:55:29.136
I must've left it down there
when I went to relight the pilot?

490
00:55:29.220 --> 00:55:31.556
Logan, your phone
has been missing for days.

491
00:55:31.639 --> 00:55:33.933
You just went to check the pilot
last night.

492
00:55:35.476 --> 00:55:36.519
What's your point?

493
00:55:37.061 --> 00:55:38.729
And then I found this...

494
00:55:42.275 --> 00:55:43.568
in the trash.

495
00:55:52.868 --> 00:55:54.411
No. I didn't do that.

496
00:55:54.995 --> 00:55:56.788
Have you been messing with me?

497
00:55:56.872 --> 00:55:58.999
Have I been messing with you?
Are you kidding me?

498
00:55:59.082 --> 00:56:01.084
No, I'm not an idiot, Logan.

499
00:56:01.418 --> 00:56:04.629
First the basement door,
and then the water heater, and now this?

500
00:56:04.713 --> 00:56:05.672
What you talking about?

501
00:56:05.755 --> 00:56:08.008
Is it because you're pissed at me?
I don't know.

502
00:56:08.300 --> 00:56:12.469
Because I have so much on my plate
right now that I can't deal with you too.

503
00:56:12.553 --> 00:56:15.014
I didn't do anything, Mom.
You're completely fucking insane.

504
00:56:15.097 --> 00:56:17.141
- Excuse me?
- Just get out of my room.

505
00:56:17.224 --> 00:56:19.143
- No. What'd you say?
- Get the fuck outta my room.

506
00:56:19.226 --> 00:56:22.563
No! You do not get to talk to me
like that. I am your mother,

507
00:56:22.646 --> 00:56:24.523
and I'm allowed to be upset.

508
00:56:26.233 --> 00:56:27.651
I know this sucks.

509
00:56:28.402 --> 00:56:31.113
I know it's not what you wanted,
'cause guess what?

510
00:56:31.196 --> 00:56:34.074
It's not what I wanted either.
So grow up, Logan.

511
00:56:36.951 --> 00:56:38.786
I fucking hate you.

512
00:56:39.829 --> 00:56:42.540
All you do is put your shit
on other people.

513
00:56:42.624 --> 00:56:44.959
Dad's gone, and you don't even care.

514
00:56:45.043 --> 00:56:48.046
He died in front of me. You haven't
asked me one time if I'm okay.

515
00:56:48.171 --> 00:56:50.548
You dragged me out of school,
brought us to this shitty town.

516
00:56:50.632 --> 00:56:52.008
You don't care if I'm okay with it.

517
00:56:52.091 --> 00:56:55.386
We wouldn't be in this situation
if Dad was still here.

518
00:56:59.891 --> 00:57:01.934
Wanna be an adult and know the truth?

519
00:57:03.101 --> 00:57:08.231
Your father is the exact reason
that we are in this situation.

520
00:57:08.315 --> 00:57:11.318
Your father left us with nothing,

521
00:57:11.401 --> 00:57:12.945
because he was irresponsible,

522
00:57:13.028 --> 00:57:16.281
and he couldn't care less about me
or about you!

523
00:57:19.201 --> 00:57:20.535
I fucking wish it was you.

524
00:58:10.417 --> 00:58:11.251
Hello?

525
00:59:17.272 --> 00:59:18.106
Oh, my God.

526
00:59:20.067 --> 00:59:21.443
Hey, Dad!

527
00:59:22.694 --> 00:59:24.237
No, no! Dad!

528
00:59:24.321 --> 00:59:25.989
Dad! No!

529
00:59:27.157 --> 00:59:29.576
It's okay. It's just a nightmare.
You were having a nightmare.

530
00:59:29.701 --> 00:59:30.535
What?

531
00:59:35.331 --> 00:59:37.583
We have a showing in an hour,
so we gotta go.

532
00:59:40.086 --> 00:59:42.004
Wait a minute. What time is it?

533
00:59:42.088 --> 00:59:43.089
1:00 p. m.

534
00:59:43.672 --> 00:59:44.757
You slept all day.

535
00:59:52.306 --> 00:59:53.641
Logan, let's go!

536
00:59:57.394 --> 00:59:58.771
- Is your room clean?
- Yeah.

537
00:59:59.395 --> 01:00:01.356
- Where are you going?
- For a run.

538
01:00:35.347 --> 01:00:36.723
Oh!

539
01:00:36.807 --> 01:00:38.016
- Hi.
- Oh, Naomi, uh...

540
01:00:38.100 --> 01:00:39.059
- Yeah, hi.
- Sorry.

541
01:00:39.143 --> 01:00:41.228
No, no. Um... you just startled me.

542
01:00:41.311 --> 01:00:43.272
Wow. I'm so glad I ran into you again.

543
01:00:43.355 --> 01:00:45.023
- How are you?
- Good.

544
01:00:45.107 --> 01:00:47.985
I'm, uh, just picking up some photos
I had developed.

545
01:00:48.068 --> 01:00:50.736
- Oh, are you a photographer?
- It's just a hobby.

546
01:00:51.279 --> 01:00:52.864
- That's great.
- Uh-huh.

547
01:00:58.870 --> 01:01:01.414
Hey, sorry I sort of disappeared
on you last time.

548
01:01:01.497 --> 01:01:03.833
Couldn't find you.
Figured I'd just get out of your hair.

549
01:01:04.417 --> 01:01:05.334
No worries.

550
01:01:08.838 --> 01:01:10.339
I know you don't know me.

551
01:01:10.423 --> 01:01:13.301
Last thing you need right now is
some guy scaring you in the parking lot

552
01:01:13.384 --> 01:01:15.136
and stalking your house.

553
01:01:15.969 --> 01:01:18.597
I just wanted to give you my number...

554
01:01:25.604 --> 01:01:27.480
in case you guys ever need anything.

555
01:01:28.607 --> 01:01:31.067
You know I just know
you guys are new around here.

556
01:01:31.943 --> 01:01:32.944
No pressure.

557
01:01:33.528 --> 01:01:34.571
Well, thank you.

558
01:01:34.654 --> 01:01:36.406
That's very sweet of you.

559
01:02:03.557 --> 01:02:05.851
Naomi, it's Allison.
We got a call from our realtor

560
01:02:05.935 --> 01:02:08.019
that our house was broken into.
Call me.

561
01:02:08.102 --> 01:02:09.395
Logan, get in the car.

562
01:02:10.188 --> 01:02:11.356
Get in the car.

563
01:02:27.830 --> 01:02:29.082
Oh, my God.

564
01:02:32.501 --> 01:02:33.377
Mom.

565
01:03:09.370 --> 01:03:10.288
Hello?

566
01:03:11.789 --> 01:03:12.665
Hello?

567
01:03:17.628 --> 01:03:19.130
Mom, we have to call the cops.

568
01:03:27.304 --> 01:03:29.139
Ma'am, we searched the entire house.

569
01:03:29.222 --> 01:03:30.473
There's no one here.

570
01:03:30.557 --> 01:03:31.683
Did you check the basement?

571
01:03:31.766 --> 01:03:33.184
Yeah. Top to bottom.

572
01:03:33.768 --> 01:03:36.479
It's definitely creepy,
but we didn't see anything.

573
01:03:38.148 --> 01:03:39.024
Mom...

574
01:03:40.692 --> 01:03:43.486
Uh, well, we had an open house here
a few days ago,

575
01:03:43.570 --> 01:03:47.157
so maybe someone found
a spare key laying around, or...

576
01:03:47.782 --> 01:03:49.116
Or maybe someone stayed.

577
01:03:53.287 --> 01:03:56.623
I know it sounds stupid, but other things
have happened before this.

578
01:03:56.707 --> 01:03:59.376
Things moving from one room to another.
Weird phone calls.

579
01:03:59.835 --> 01:04:01.086
From anyone in particular?

580
01:04:01.462 --> 01:04:03.380
No. No one would respond.

581
01:04:05.799 --> 01:04:07.468
Don't look at her. I'm not lying.

582
01:04:08.552 --> 01:04:09.386
Okay, look.

583
01:04:10.262 --> 01:04:13.390
I know that we probably sound
like the crazy new people in town,

584
01:04:13.474 --> 01:04:17.310
but this is my sister's house, and we're
supposed to be taking care of it, so...

585
01:04:17.393 --> 01:04:20.313
Look, I understand the fear
in these situations.

586
01:04:20.396 --> 01:04:21.522
Okay? I do.

587
01:04:21.981 --> 01:04:25.068
But it's likely the front door was
unlocked and some kids snuck in.

588
01:04:25.151 --> 01:04:26.527
Are you kidding me?

589
01:04:27.737 --> 01:04:29.489
Look at this.
You think some kids did this?

590
01:04:29.572 --> 01:04:32.325
It's not uncommon. Okay?
Kids get bored. They do weird things.

591
01:04:32.408 --> 01:04:34.369
They were probably trying to scare
the newcomers.

592
01:04:38.039 --> 01:04:39.623
Okay.

593
01:04:40.499 --> 01:04:42.042
Is there nothing else you can do?

594
01:04:44.461 --> 01:04:47.047
If it makes you feel any better,
we can come by in the morning.

595
01:04:47.130 --> 01:04:49.299
Yeah. Yeah, please do.

596
01:04:51.258 --> 01:04:52.134
Okay.

597
01:04:52.676 --> 01:04:53.511
Let's go.

598
01:04:54.970 --> 01:04:56.222
You all have a good one.

599
01:05:06.689 --> 01:05:08.108
We have to stay in a hotel.

600
01:05:08.191 --> 01:05:09.651
Honey, we're fine.

601
01:05:09.734 --> 01:05:12.987
No, Mom. Something is clearly going on.

602
01:05:13.696 --> 01:05:16.199
Look, I know you think I did
all that shit before, but I didn't.

603
01:05:16.282 --> 01:05:19.869
- I swear to God.
- Okay. No, but you heard them.

604
01:05:19.953 --> 01:05:21.496
There's nothing to worry about.

605
01:05:21.579 --> 01:05:22.789
Mom, please.

606
01:05:22.872 --> 01:05:25.667
Logan, we can't afford it right now.

607
01:05:26.501 --> 01:05:27.335
Okay?

608
01:05:31.380 --> 01:05:32.423
We're fine.

609
01:06:13.671 --> 01:06:14.505
Hey.

610
01:06:19.844 --> 01:06:20.720
Mom...

611
01:06:22.012 --> 01:06:23.680
- I'm going to bed.
- Okay.

612
01:06:26.600 --> 01:06:27.517
You all right?

613
01:06:31.521 --> 01:06:32.522
Yeah, I'm fine.

614
01:06:35.400 --> 01:06:36.985
You wanna stay in here tonight?

615
01:06:43.492 --> 01:06:44.409
Sure.

616
01:07:00.716 --> 01:07:01.800
What is this?

617
01:07:02.968 --> 01:07:06.013
It's just the guy from the store.

618
01:07:08.182 --> 01:07:10.684
He gave it to me
in case we ever needed anything.

619
01:07:11.185 --> 01:07:12.685
He was just being friendly.

620
01:07:13.269 --> 01:07:14.938
You can throw it out if you want.

621
01:07:16.231 --> 01:07:17.190
I don't care.

622
01:07:22.779 --> 01:07:24.030
I'm gonna go brush my teeth.

623
01:07:24.531 --> 01:07:25.365
Okay.

624
01:07:44.174 --> 01:07:45.050
Logan?

625
01:08:05.987 --> 01:08:06.821
Hey.

626
01:08:07.822 --> 01:08:10.074
Chris. What are you doing here?

627
01:08:10.157 --> 01:08:11.325
Uh, Mom.

628
01:08:11.409 --> 01:08:13.160
It's okay. I called him.

629
01:08:17.456 --> 01:08:19.458
The cops weren't worried at all, huh?

630
01:08:20.751 --> 01:08:21.586
No.

631
01:08:22.712 --> 01:08:26.090
- They said some kids probably did it.
- Well, that's possible.

632
01:08:26.716 --> 01:08:28.551
A lot of them are assholes up here.

633
01:08:31.928 --> 01:08:33.305
It didn't feel like kids.

634
01:08:36.391 --> 01:08:37.767
Oh, what did it feel like?

635
01:08:41.271 --> 01:08:42.147
Like...

636
01:08:43.565 --> 01:08:44.482
personal.

637
01:08:48.069 --> 01:08:49.779
Like someone had been here before.

638
01:08:52.240 --> 01:08:54.367
I don't know. Maybe I'm... maybe I'm crazy.

639
01:08:58.996 --> 01:09:01.206
Well, it's just the two of you
up here, huh?

640
01:09:04.918 --> 01:09:05.794
Yeah.

641
01:09:25.480 --> 01:09:26.564
Anything?

642
01:09:27.774 --> 01:09:28.650
All clear.

643
01:09:32.570 --> 01:09:33.446
Thank you.

644
01:09:34.113 --> 01:09:34.989
Yeah.

645
01:09:42.330 --> 01:09:43.790
- Hey.
- Oh.

646
01:09:44.874 --> 01:09:47.376
- Appreciate it.
- Yeah. Need anything else?

647
01:09:48.251 --> 01:09:49.753
Uh, no, I'm good, buddy.

648
01:09:50.379 --> 01:09:51.713
Yeah. Go get some rest.

649
01:09:53.840 --> 01:09:56.051
Hey, thank you for doing this.

650
01:09:57.594 --> 01:09:58.845
Yeah. Not a problem.

651
01:10:00.430 --> 01:10:02.641
Look, this place is weird sometimes.

652
01:10:03.308 --> 01:10:05.435
Yeah, it took me a while
to get used to it, too.

653
01:10:06.895 --> 01:10:08.563
I'm sure it's nothing, but, uh...

654
01:10:09.731 --> 01:10:10.649
I'll be here.

655
01:10:13.901 --> 01:10:15.277
I'm sorry, um...

656
01:10:16.195 --> 01:10:19.990
- if I was rude before. I just...
- No, no, no, no. No need to explain, man.

657
01:10:20.074 --> 01:10:21.158
We're all good.

658
01:10:23.202 --> 01:10:24.495
- Night.
- Night.

659
01:11:10.998 --> 01:11:11.874
Chris?

660
01:11:40.943 --> 01:11:41.819
Chris?

661
01:12:05.926 --> 01:12:07.177
Chris. Chris!

662
01:12:07.719 --> 01:12:08.553
Chris!

663
01:15:35.419 --> 01:15:36.461
Logan...

664
01:16:18.334 --> 01:16:19.419
No.

665
01:16:21.838 --> 01:16:22.756
No.

666
01:16:28.344 --> 01:16:29.220
Logan.

667
01:16:31.389 --> 01:16:32.348
Logan?

668
01:16:41.606 --> 01:16:43.232
No, no!

669
01:16:43.691 --> 01:16:44.817
No.

670
01:16:47.153 --> 01:16:49.363
Aah... aah. Aah.

671
01:16:53.993 --> 01:16:55.912
No. Please, no.

672
01:16:56.746 --> 01:16:58.331
Please, no.

673
01:16:59.581 --> 01:17:00.791
Logan!

674
01:17:30.444 --> 01:17:32.071
No! No!

675
01:17:43.541 --> 01:17:45.543
No!

676
01:18:03.685 --> 01:18:04.561
Fuck.

677
01:18:06.896 --> 01:18:09.816
Logan!

678
01:18:19.700 --> 01:18:21.243
Hey, Mom! Mom!

679
01:18:22.536 --> 01:18:23.370
Mom?

680
01:18:32.671 --> 01:18:33.672
Mom!

681
01:18:34.548 --> 01:18:35.966
Mom, hey.

682
01:18:36.633 --> 01:18:38.635
Mom! Mom, what happened?

683
01:18:38.719 --> 01:18:40.387
- Look at me.
- Logan.

684
01:18:40.470 --> 01:18:41.929
Here, get up.

685
01:18:42.013 --> 01:18:43.764
Get up. Come on.

686
01:18:44.724 --> 01:18:46.934
You're so cold.

687
01:18:47.018 --> 01:18:49.061
What did he do?
What did he do to you?

688
01:18:49.145 --> 01:18:51.314
I should have listened to you.

689
01:18:51.939 --> 01:18:52.940
Where's Chris?

690
01:18:53.900 --> 01:18:55.026
He's dead.

691
01:18:56.277 --> 01:18:58.279
What? Oh, my God.

692
01:19:00.615 --> 01:19:01.449
Oh, no.

693
01:19:01.908 --> 01:19:03.284
He's gonna come back.

694
01:19:03.576 --> 01:19:06.037
We have to get out.
We're gonna get out. Okay?

695
01:19:06.120 --> 01:19:07.245
Yeah, yeah.

696
01:19:09.122 --> 01:19:11.708
Look at me.
We're gonna call the cops.

697
01:19:11.791 --> 01:19:14.085
- I don't have a phone.
- I need to go downstairs, Mom.

698
01:19:14.169 --> 01:19:16.922
- No, baby. No!
- Hey, I'm gonna be fine.

699
01:19:17.005 --> 01:19:20.091
I'm gonna be fine, okay? I love you.

700
01:19:20.425 --> 01:19:21.384
Mom.

701
01:19:22.928 --> 01:19:24.137
I love you so much.

702
01:19:27.098 --> 01:19:28.558
I love you, baby.

703
01:20:42.254 --> 01:20:43.338
You say, "Hey"

704
01:21:19.080 --> 01:21:19.914
No.

705
01:21:23.335 --> 01:21:26.087
Logan!

706
01:21:43.812 --> 01:21:44.855
Mom! Mom?

707
01:21:45.606 --> 01:21:46.565
Help!

708
01:21:54.990 --> 01:21:56.992
Logan!

709
01:23:50.851 --> 01:23:51.810
Mom?

710
01:24:11.872 --> 01:24:13.206
Logan!

711
01:24:22.548 --> 01:24:23.674
Mom?

712
01:24:24.675 --> 01:24:25.510
Mom?

713
01:24:26.761 --> 01:24:27.595
No.

714
01:24:31.390 --> 01:24:33.476
Run! Run!

715
01:24:33.559 --> 01:24:34.602
No! Mom!

716
01:25:25.442 --> 01:25:26.277
No!

717
01:25:28.903 --> 01:25:30.905
- No!
- Now run!

718
01:26:03.520 --> 01:26:04.396
Help!

719
01:26:06.607 --> 01:26:08.275
Somebody help me!

720
01:26:10.110 --> 01:26:10.944
Aah!

721
01:28:50.597 --> 01:28:51.431
Please!

722
01:28:52.140 --> 01:28:53.474
Don't hurt me! Please.

723
01:28:54.016 --> 01:28:56.727
No! Don't hurt me! No!

724
01:28:56.810 --> 01:28:58.103
No!
